42-reset-and-stale-symbol: a module of the same name after curry.reset and
curry.reload, and a symbol that outlives the reset.

Seam: curry.compile under one modulename three times across a soft reset
and a hard reset; the module objects and the symbols kept alive in Python.
Sources: memo A13, A17; catalogue P30, P35; issue #114 (open).
Backends: cxx.  The Python backend differs on the old symbols: there
first.f stays 1 and second.f stays 2 after the resets.  Oracle: none.

Expected output pins today's behaviour of #114 on the C++ backend: after
the reset, second.f is 2 (the first symptom, fixed at 3d79a27e) and the
old symbol first.f evaluates to 2 as well; after the reload, first.f and
second.f both evaluate to 3, the code of the newest module of that name.
curry.modules holds the Prelude after reset and is empty right after
reload, until the next import.  A fixed system refuses the evaluation of
first.f after the reset with an error (the expectation of #114); the lines
"first.f after the reset", "second.f after the reload" and "first.f after
the reload" change then.
